{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792795225,"nonce":"poKXsHICWX9jiRPj917qei65//4=","title":"Add browser media guests for Jam collaborators and playtesters","message":"Master roadmap: 455de32231e2b4a39765b4dff0223570b525ccec145049431e6483f5aa521f98\n\nMilestone: P3\n\nScope\nImplement a scoped browser join flow for invited artists, musicians and playtesters: identity/invite validation, participant list, team chat, microphone/camera/screen permissions and reconnect/leave. Reuse the room/media contracts and respect guest/host billing rules. The initial browser client is a media/presence guest; a full browser code editor is separate later scope. Evaluate plain WebRTC/SFU versus supported SDKs without changing native client requirements.\n\nAcceptance criteria\nAn invited browser guest can join a native room without a streaming-platform account or paid subscription. Expired/reused invites, revoked guests, unsupported capture, denied devices and refresh/reconnect behave correctly. Browser identity grants no implicit file, terminal or public-broadcast access; media cleanup and quota attribution are tested.\n\nAssociations and blocking dependencies are recorded below using full git-bug IDs. This issue remains open until implementation and validation are complete.","files":null}]}